 This install applies to "Slicks'n'Slide", a native Amiga port of the DOS
 shareware racing game by Timo Kauppinen.


 Requirements:
 -------------
 Standalone: PAL A1200, 68020, AGA, 2 MiB Chip RAM, AmigaOS 3.x and SetPatch.
 Installation requires Installer V43 or later; IconX launches Play from
 Workbench. These are Amiga system tools, not included in this archive.
 Close other applications on a 2 MiB machine. Allow about 1 MB free RAM for
 the extraction helper, at least 2 MB temporary disk space and 3 MB
 destination space. Do not choose RAM: or T: as the temporary drawer on a
 memory-constrained Amiga.

 The optional WHDLoad icon requires WHDLoad version 17.0 or better and extra
 Fast RAM. The slave reserves 2 MiB ChipMem plus 1 MiB expansion memory and
 512 KiB Kickstart space; the host system, WHDLoad and PRELOAD need additional
 memory. Tested with 2 MiB Chip and 4 MiB Fast RAM, including PRELOAD.

 WHDLoad also requires a legally obtained Kickstart 3.1 image and matching
 relocation file in "Devs:Kickstarts" or "WHDCOMMON:". Supported pairs are:

   kick40063.A600  and kick40063.A600.RTB
   kick40068.A1200 and kick40068.A1200.RTB
   kick40068.A4000 and kick40068.A4000.RTB

 Standalone play does not need WHDLoad or a Kickstart image. Neither the
 Kickstart images nor the original game data are included in this package.


 Installation:
 -------------
 Download the original shareware Slix151.zip from:

 https://www.slicksnslide.com/webapi/download.php?p=dos-slix&v=Slix151.zip

 Leave it compressed. Unpack this LHA, open its drawer and run the Install
 icon; select the ZIP when asked. The self-contained helper checks the
 supported publisher ZIP before extracting the two data files and 195 tracks.
 It never installs the DOS executable, DOSBox, configuration or a
 registration key. No host computer, UnZip utility or PC emulator is needed.

 Choose Keep when asked about existing data to preserve modified tracks and
 records; Reinstall replaces the 195 supplied tracks and both data files.
 Updating the port keeps keys and saves. Failed extraction does not replace
 installed files. If copying fails due to disk space, retain the staging
 drawer and rerun the installer.


 Display:
 --------
 The original 320x200 picture is shown on a PAL 50 Hz AGA screen. Race
 physics and lap clocks run on the original real-time clock at any frame
 rate. Frames that take longer than one refresh are shown immediately rather
 than waiting for the next one, which can briefly tear moving objects.


 Playing and quitting:
 ---------------------
 Double-click Play for standalone, or SlicksWHDLoad if you chose that option.
 From a Shell: CD to the installed Slicks drawer, then Execute Play.
 The installed data/ drawer holds the native executable, original data,
 tracks, configuration, driver profiles, saved championships and an optional
 SLICKS.REK. Both launch methods share these files; keep the drawer writable.

 Exit through the game's menu to save pending changes. WHDLoad's QuitKey
 (F10) exits immediately and cannot perform deferred game saves.


 Features:
 ---------
 - the complete original game: single races, championships, shop, weapons,
   demos, help, options and all eight languages
 - original graphics, fonts, tracks and sounds from the publisher's data
 - native 68020 code, AGA display and four-channel Paula sound
 - original real-time race clock at any frame rate
 - digital Amiga joysticks in both game ports


 Controls:
 ---------
 Menus: arrows, Enter, Escape; F1 for help. Configure drivers and controls in
 the original menus. Page Up/Down in menus and help: keypad 9/3, or the two
 keys immediately right of P ([ and ] on a US keyboard). Amiga Help
 replaces PC Scroll Lock for shop screenshots.
 Joystick 1 is the usual joystick port, joystick 2 the mouse port. PC
 parallel-port joystick adapters are not available on the Amiga.


 Registration:
 -------------
 Support the original author by registering. Place your own valid SLICKS.REK
 in the installed data/ drawer. Shareware restrictions and reminders remain
 without it; a valid key enables the original registered functionality.
 Invalid keys are rejected. This package contains no key or bypass.


